<article class="env-lemma" id="0F8W">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0F8W">Lemma <span data-tag="0F8W">38.43.9</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/0F8S" data-tag="0F8S">38.43.1</a> let $W \subset X$ be the maximal open subscheme over which the cohomology sheaves of $M$ are locally free. Then the morphism $b : X' \to X$ of Lemma <a href="/tag/0GTY" data-tag="0GTY">38.43.6</a> is an isomorphism over $W$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is true because for any affine chart $(U, A, f, M^\bullet )$ with $U \subset W$ we have that $I_ i(M^\bullet , f)$ are locally generated by a power of $f$ by More on Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/0GSV" data-tag="0GSV">15.98.4</a>. Since $f$ is a nonzerodivisor, the blowing up $b^{-1}(U) \to U$ is an isomorphism. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>